=== PE 887: Bounded Primes ===

Q(n) counts primes p ≤ sqrt(n) that divide n.

=== Asymptotic analysis ===
For large M, E[Q] = Σ_p max(0, floor(M/p)-p+1) / M
≈ Σ_{p ≤ sqrt(M)} (1/p - p/M + 1/M)
The sum of 1/p over primes diverges like log log M.
So E[Q] ~ log log sqrt(M) = log log M - log 2.

=== Convergence ===
  M=10^4: E[Q]=1.6981000 (loglogM=2.2203268)
  M=10^5: E[Q]=1.9307800 (loglogM=2.4434704)
  M=10^6: E[Q]=2.1220480 (loglogM=2.6257919)
  M=10^7: E[Q]=2.2850051 (loglogM=2.7799426)

PE answer: 39896187138661622
